Build a complete Python Face Recognition Attendance System.

Project name: Face Recognition Attendance System.

Requirements:

1. Create a clean and modern desktop GUI using Tkinter.
2. Add a "Register Student" option.
3. Registration should ask for:
   - Student Name
   - Student ID
4. Open the webcam and capture multiple face images of the student.
5. Store the captured images inside a dataset folder.
6. Create face encodings from the registered images.
7. Add a "Start Attendance" button.
8. Open the webcam and recognize registered students in real time.
9. When a known student is recognized, automatically mark attendance.
10. Store attendance in attendance/attendance.csv with:
    - Student ID
    - Student Name
    - Date
    - Time
    - Status
11. A student must not be marked twice on the same date.
12. Add an "Attendance Report" button to display attendance records.
13. Add a "Search Student" feature.
14. Add an "Exit" button.
15. Show the recognized student's name and ID on the webcam screen.
16. Display "Unknown Face" when the face is not registered.
17. Handle cases where the webcam is unavailable.
18. Handle duplicate student IDs.
19. Handle missing or corrupted images gracefully.
20. Keep the code modular and well commented.

Use:
- Python 3
- OpenCV
- face_recognition
- NumPy
- Pandas
- Tkinter
- CSV or SQLite

Create all required files automatically and provide:
- requirements.txt
- complete source code
- folder structure
- installation commands
- run commands

Make the application beginner-friendly and suitable as a college project.

